      "worked": "Let $f(x)=3e^x-2$.\n\n$$\\begin{align*}f'(x)&=3e^x\\\\f'(0)&=3e^0\\\\f'(0)&=3\\end{align*}$$\n\nThe tangent gradient is $m_T=3$.\n\n$$\\begin{align*}f(0)&=3e^0-2\\\\f(0)&=1\\end{align*}$$\n\nUse the point-gradient formula with point $(0,1)$:\n\n$$\\begin{align*}y-1&=3(x-0)\\\\y&=3x+1\\end{align*}$$",
